WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.700
Consider looking at yourself in the mirror.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.220
Have you ever looked so closely and intensely
at your reflection that you start to become

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:19.020
aware of the details and complexities of your
skin that you otherwise never notice?

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:25.300
Have you ever stared at your reflection until
you no longer recognize it?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.600
What is it that you are looking at it?

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.420
Is it YOU?

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.360
Are YOU your face?

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.590
Are YOU your brain?

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:40.500
Do you control entirely what it is that you
are looking at?

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.630
If it decides to grow hair, do you have any
say in the matter?

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:51.890
You can cut or shave the hair, but it will
still continue to grow.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:57.070
What you are staring at is, therefore, not
entirely yours.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:02.190
It belongs partly to the collective entity
of life.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:08.390
What you are staring at is part stranger to
you, and you must make friends with it or

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.869
it will become your worst enemy.

00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:17.249
As humans, we are just as unconscious as we
are conscious.

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:23.140
For everything that we can control and understand
about ourselves, there is an equal amount

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.289
that we cannot.

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:31.349
We sit somewhere in the middle, between complete
consciousness and complete unconsciousness,

00:01:31.349 --> 00:01:38.319
and this is arguably where all human conflict
stems from.

00:01:38.319 --> 00:01:44.969
Smart enough to understand the notion of complete
control and perfection, but not smart enough

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:47.209
to achieve it.

00:01:47.209 --> 00:01:52.749
We have yet to become what we conceive and
expect of ourselves.

00:01:52.749 --> 00:01:59.310
But no matter how hard we try, at this point
in evolution, we will never be of complete

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.880
and perfect omniscience.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:08.459
We all know this, yet it still seems that
we constantly expect perfection from our self

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:11.300
and the rest of the world.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:17.970
But we must not depend our purpose and excitement
in life on whether or not we can control and

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.180
perfect everything.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:26.970
Our sense of purpose and excitement is found
in the way that our imperfection keeps life

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:31.150
fresh, uncertain, and inspiring.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:39.030
Only those who can posses the conscious abilities
of the human, but not be tormented by the

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:46.650
conscious inabilities of the human, will become
into what it truly means to be human in the

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.890
first place.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:55.860
We must learn how to separate the desire of
perfection and the expectation of perfection.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:03.660
It is admirable and very human to strive for
perfection, but it is equally human to not

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.830
achieve it.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:12.690
We must remember this as we travel through
life, so that we do not become disheartened

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.860
and void of wonder and enjoyment.

